      "description": "Recent Jobs\n        - Ferris State University Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Location Closes Recreation Center Student Mngr (Student Position) Big Rapids, MI 49307 6 Sep 2026 The Student Manager for the Student Recreation Center is responsible for the overall operation of the recreational facility, ensuring a safe, inclusive, and engaging environment for all students, members, and guests. This position involves overseeing student staff, managing programming, providing excellent customer service, enforcing policies and procedures, and following risk management procedures. Vice President Governmental & External Affairs Big Rapids, MI 49307 The Vice President for Governmental Relations & External Affairs provides strategic leadership for the University’s governmental relations, external affairs, and public policy efforts.  Reporting to the President, this position serves as the University’s principal liaison with federal, state, and local government officials and agencies and works to advance the University’s mission, priorities, and interests through effective government and community engagement. The Vice President develops and implements comprehensive governmental relations strategies; monitors legislative and regulatory developments; builds and maintains relationships with elected and appointed officials; and represents the University before governmental entities and other external stakeholders.  The position works closely with the President, Board of Trustees, senior leaders, faculty, staff, students, and external partners to identify opportunities, assess potential impacts of public policy, and coordinate the University’s response to legislative and regulatory issues. The Vice President also leads efforts to identify and pursue public funding opportunities, including state and federal appropriations, grants, capital projects, and other governmental resources that support the University’s strategic priorities.  This position may have a primary work location in both Lansing and Big Rapids. The Vice President, in collaboration with the President, will build strategic relationships with businesses and corporations throughout Michigan, with a particular focus on Southeast and West Michigan. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Assistant Director of Residential Programs and Services Big Rapids, MI 49307 Provide primary responsibility for the administration of the Residence Halls, Apartments, and Suites on campus.  Provide leadership and supervision for residential programs and services.  Assist in the development and implementation of comprehensive policies and procedures for on-campus housing operations. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future.  The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Required: Bachelor’s degree in personnel administration, counseling, or related field. 3-5 years of work experience in University housing and residence life with responsibilities which involved supervision (student or professional), corrective action, conflict resolution, and programming in a University setting. LGBTQ+ Resource Student Asst (Student Position) Big Rapids, MI 49307 1 Nov 2026 The LGBTQ+ resource center is seeking a student assistant. In this position, you will greet students and offer them resources. Adjunct Instructor - Writing Center Specialist (Part Time) Big Rapids, MI 49307 Writing Center Specialists provide writing consultation (on-site and electronic/digital) to undergraduate and graduate students for 10 to 28 hours per week. The successful applicant will be familiar with APA and MLA documentation and must be comfortable working one-on-one with a diverse student population representing a full range of majors and writing skills, from remedial to advanced. The successful applicant must be comfortable working in face-to-face and electronic/digital instructional settings. This is a pooled position. One or more applicants may be hired to assist students on a semester-by-semester basis. The anticipated start date of this position will be throughout the academic year, with some initial appointments in September 2026. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Required: Bachelor’s degree in English, English Education, History, Social Sciences, or a related field. One year of experience involving tutoring and teaching at the K-12 and/or college level. Experience working with diverse populations, including ESL. Food Service Worker Big Rapids, MI 49307 A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at Erbert & Gerbert's. The normal working hours are 5:00 a.m. to 1:30 p.m., Sunday through Thursday. Days off are Friday and Saturday. The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation. Food Service Worker Big Rapids, MI 49307 A Food Service Worker position is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 6:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m. Sunday through Thursday. Days off are Friday and Saturday.  However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position.  NOTE: Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation. Temporary Food Service Worker Big Rapids, MI 49307 A position classified as a Temporary Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 6 a.m. - 2:30 pm, Tuesday through Saturday.  Days off are Sunday and Monday.  The exact duration of this temporary position is undetermined at this time, but it will not exceed one year.  This position will begin on September 15, or sooner, subject to approval. However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation. Temporary Food Service Worker Big Rapids, MI 49307 A position classified as a Temporary Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Café. The normal working hours are 1:30pm-10:00pm Sunday, Monday and Thursday through Saturday.  Days off are Tuesday and Wednesday. The exact duration of this temporary position is undetermined at this time.  The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends.  If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation. Part-Time Bus Driver Big Rapids, MI 49307 Provide safe transportation for passengers, equipment, and packages. Assist in maintenance of University owned and leased vehicles. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Valid Michigan commercial driver’s license (CDL), Group A or B with endorsements ‘P’ with no restrictions, airbrakes and DOT medical card. Three years full-time equivalent of combined bus and heavy equipment truck driving, with emphasis on bus driving experience. Demonstrated experience with minor automotive repair and driving all types of vehicles. Part Time Temporary Personal Counselor Big Rapids, MI 49307 This is a temporary, part time clinical position. The position will provide individual and group short-term mental health counseling and crisis intervention for Ferris State University (FSU) students. This position will end following the fall semester (December 11, 2026) This position may not work more than 28 hours per week. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F1 EAD’s, OPT, H1B, etc.. Required: Master's Degree in Professional Counseling, and/or Counseling Psychology, and/or Clinical Psychology, and/or Social Work, and/or Marriage and Family Therapy and/or comparable mental health professional degree. Active license (or application for license pending) to practice in the state of Michigan, LMSW and/or LLP and/or LPC and/or LP, TLLP or LLPC, LLMSW. Demonstrated experience in counseling clients with a wide range of psychological and emotional health concerns. Torch Freelance Reporter (Student Position) Big Rapids, MI 49307 12 Dec 2026 The Torch is looking for a freelance porter. This position may be your opportunity to use your skills as well as gain further experience. CAPS Clerical 1 (Student Position) Big Rapids, MI 49307 18 Sep 2026 Want to get exposed to everything that Ferris State has to offer? Career and Professional Success! You will get to help out at many events across campus, create advertisements, and other clerical duties. Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position) Big Rapids, MI 49307 12 Dec 2026 Support daily operations of School of Digital Media labs—enforcing lab rules, maintaining equipment, managing seat reservations/usage—and assist in other program‑specific tasks.\n\nDAGD Lab: Advising students on software operation. Guiding, advising and consulting on projects. Maintaining order in the labs.\nEsports Lab: Assisting production and content team to create media for social media and broadcasts. Assistant Professor - Economics (9 Mos Tenure Track) Big Rapids, MI 49307 The College of Business at Ferris State University seeks a diverse group of outstanding applicants for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Economics. Teaching will include economics undergraduate and graduate courses. Candidates are expected to foster a meaningful learning experience for our students; faculty are expected to be student-oriented, advise, and integrate current technology into the learning environment. Additionally, faculty will participate in collaborative efforts to advance curricular initiatives, participate in the assessment of student learning, and further develop programmatic enhancements. Specifically, we expect the candidate to be willing to engage students outside the classroom, support and expand our existing academic initiatives, and mentor students beyond a traditional academic advising role. In support of teaching, faculty will engage in scholarly/professional activities and participate in department, college, and university committees. The selected candidate should be willing to serve as a program coordinator. Off-campus and online teaching may be required. Courses are to be taught in person on one of Ferris State University's Campuses or online. The candidate selected for the position must reside in Michigan after acceptance of employment and will perform duties at a Ferris site. The anticipated start date of this position is January 2027 at the earliest and August 2027 at the latest. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H-1 B, etc. Dispatch Specialist Big Rapids, MI 49307 Coordinate the Public Safety Department communication system and perform a variety of police records support functions, some of which require special certification. This position will be expected to work different/longer hours during times of emergency. This is a CTA-MEA/NEA position. Required: Associate’s Degree. LEIN certified or achieve such certification within 60 days of hire. Six months work experience in dispatching, law enforcement, or as an equivalent emergency communication professional. Custodian Big Rapids, MI 49307 Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. This position is M-F, 5:00 pm - 1:30 am. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Valid driver's license. Custodial/janitorial work experience in a commercial/hospital/school environment in a commercial cleaning service or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training. Custodian Big Rapids, MI 49307 Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. The anticipated schedule for this position will be Sa-W, 6:00 am – 2:30 pm. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Valid driver's license. Custodial/Janitorial work experience in a commercial-hospital-school environment, in a commercial cleaning service, or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training. Demonstrated experience with correct operation of a variety of commercial custodial equipment such as a vacuum cleaner, automatic scrubber, high-speed burnisher, single-disc scrubber, carpet extraction/shampoo equipment, or other essential or similar custodial equipment. Food Service Worker Big Rapids, MI 49307 A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 1:30pm-10pm Sunday through Wednesday and Saturday.  Days off are Thursday and Friday. This position will begin as soon as possible, subject to manager approval.  However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation. Part-Time Custodian (Racquet & Fitness Center) Big Rapids, MI 49307 A position classified as a part-time custodian is available with the Facilities Management department in the Racquet & Fitness Center. The work schedule will be 20 hours per week and will not exceed 28 hours a week. The normal working hours are 10:00 pm - 2:00 am, Monday through Friday. However, work may be required at other times including evenings/weekends. It is not anticipated that this position will become full-time. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University's requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Valid driver's license. No custodial work experience required – will train selected applicant. More Jobs 176 Expression of Interest Loading... Current Opportunities Position Location Closes Recreation Center Student Mngr (Student Position) Big Rapids, MI 49307 6 Sep 2026 The Student Manager for the Student Recreation Center is responsible for the overall operation of the recreational facility, ensuring a safe, inclusive, and engaging environment for all students, members, and guests. This position involves overseeing student staff, managing programming, providing excellent customer service, enforcing policies and procedures, and following risk management procedures. Vice President Governmental & External Affairs Big Rapids, MI 49307 The Vice President for Governmental Relations & External Affairs provides strategic leadership for the University’s governmental relations, external affairs, and public policy efforts.  Reporting to the President, this position serves as the University’s principal liaison with federal, state, and local government officials and agencies and works to advance the University’s mission, priorities, and interests through effective government and community engagement. The Vice President develops and implements comprehens