    "https://jobs.ferris.edu/en-us/job/498191/esports-and-digital-lab-monitor-student-position": {
      "title": "Details - Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position)\n        - Ferris State University",
      "description": "Details - Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position)\n        - Ferris State University Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position) Apply now Job no: 498191 Work type: Student Employment - General Location: Big Rapids, MI 49307 Categories: Student Employment - General Position Title: Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position) Location: Big Rapids, MI Department: School of Digital Media Advertised Salary: $14.00 Summary of Position: Support daily operations of School of Digital Media labs—enforcing lab rules, maintaining equipment, managing seat reservations/usage—and assist in other program‑specific tasks. DAGD Lab: Advising students on software operation. Guiding, advising and consulting on projects. Maintaining order in the labs. Esports Lab: Assisting production and content team to create media for social media and broadcasts. Position Type: Student Position Position Requirements: Familiarity with the rules, practices, and workflows of collegiate digital media labs such as esports or Digital Animation and Game Design (DAGD) • Basic computer‑hardware and software troubleshooting skills • Excellent customer service and communication skills • Strong attention to detail • Some understanding of Ferris State University structures and resources • Availability to work scheduled shifts from Esports Lab Hours - 4 PM–12 AM on weekdays and 12 PM–12 AM on weekends; DAGD Lab Hours - 8 PM–12 AM on weekdays and 2pm-10PM weekends. • Preferred interest in content production and digital media; experience with social‑media and content‑creation software (Adobe Creative Suite – Photoshop, Lightroom, Premiere, After Effects – and/or DaVinci Resolve) Essential Duties/Responsibilities: • Greet and assist all participants and visitors in the labs, enforcing lab rules and safety protocols • Monitor, maintain, and troubleshoot hardware, peripherals, and workstations • Manage seat reservations, check‑in procedures, and track lab usage statistics • Maintain cleanliness and organization of the lab and equipment storage areas • Support event setup, staffing, and breakdown for program activities • Attend regular team meetings and contribute ideas for improving lab operations and strategies Other Duties May Include: • Capture and edit game clips/highlights; produce graphics and short‑form videos for social platforms (Twitter, Instagram, TikTok, YouTube) • Assist with live broadcast production, including camera setup, scene transitions, and overlay management • Coordinate with production teams to resolve audiovisual issues during streams or media projects • Assist with content creation, media production, or other program‑specific projects for esports, Digital Animation and Game Design (DAGD), or related disciplines • Other duties as assigned Number of Positions Available: 1 Documents Needed to Apply: Resume, Class Schedule Please include a sample of your content work (e.g., link to portfolio or social media channels). Be prepared to provide your weekly availability schedule when contacted for an interview. Job Close Date: December 12, 2026 EEO Statement: Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.  Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at ferris.edu . The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit: Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement . Advertised: 31 Aug 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 12 Dec 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like t