      "title": "",
      "description": "<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"utf-8\"?><rss xmlns:a10=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\" version=\"2.0\"><channel xmlns:job=\"http://pageuppeople.com/\"><title /><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/listing/</link><description /><a10:link rel=\"self\" href=\"https://jobs.ferris.edu/1010/cw/en-us/latest_jobs.rss\" /><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498196</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498196</link><title>Recreation Center Student Mngr (Student Position)</title><description>The Student Manager for the Student Recreation Center is responsible for the overall operation of the recreational facility, ensuring a safe, inclusive, and engaging environment for all students, members, and guests. This position involves overseeing student staff, managing programming, providing excellent customer service, enforcing policies and procedures, and following risk management procedures.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498196</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;University Recreation - Student Manager (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Student Services&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00 - $14.49&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Student Manager for the Student Recreation Center is responsible for the overall operation of the recreational facility, ensuring a safe, inclusive, and engaging environment for all students, members, and guests. This position involves overseeing student staff, managing programming, providing excellent customer service, enforcing policies and procedures, and following risk management procedures.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and organizational skills.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal abilities.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently and as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Ability to resolve conflict in a respectful manner.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in leading or supervising peers and or fellow workers.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Must be able to work flexible hours including early mornings, evenings, and at least 1 weekend a month.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;As an individual who is handling money during your shift on behalf of the University, is required that Human Resources obtain your background check to determine your eligibility to handle money transactions.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Ensure the facility is clean, safe, and inclusive for all students, members and guests.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Help enforce all policies regarding students and members for entering and leaving the facility.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage the use of recreational equipment and spaces.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Help with programming throughout the facility when called upon.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Open and close the cash register to the POS system each day.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Responsible for closing the drawer each night and batching out all credit cards.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carryout all risk management procedures when needed.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Supervise, mentor, and support all student staff during scheduled shift.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Monitor staff responsibilities to ensure all tasks are being completed during shifts.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Foster a positive work environment.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Provide excellent customer service by addressing user inquiries and concerns promptly and professionally.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Handle membership registrations and other administrative tasks related to user services.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Manage user access and ensure compliance with facility policies and procedure&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Identify, troubleshoot, and resolve issues related to facility operations, staff performance, and customer satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate records of incidents and follow up as necessary.&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;September 6, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498196&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Mon, 07 Sep 2026 03:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>E - Student Affairs</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498197</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498197</link><title>Vice President Governmental &amp; External Affairs</title><description>The Vice President for Governmental Relations &amp; External Affairs provides strategic leadership for the University’s governmental relations, external affairs, and public policy efforts.  Reporting to the President, this position serves as the University’s principal liaison with federal, state, and local government officials and agencies and works to advance the University’s mission, priorities, and interests through effective government and community engagement. The Vice President develops and implements comprehensive governmental relations strategies; monitors legislative and regulatory developments; builds and maintains relationships with elected and appointed officials; and represents the University before governmental entities and other external stakeholders.  The position works closely with the President, Board of Trustees, senior leaders, faculty, staff, students, and external partners to identify opportunities, assess potential impacts of public policy, and coordinate the University’s response to legislative and regulatory issues. The Vice President also leads efforts to identify and pursue public funding opportunities, including state and federal appropriations, grants, capital projects, and other governmental resources that support the University’s strategic priorities.  This position may have a primary work location in both Lansing and Big Rapids. The Vice President, in collaboration with the President, will build strategic relationships with businesses and corporations throughout Michigan, with a particular focus on Southeast and West Michigan. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Administrative,Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498197</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 651px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Vice President Governmental &amp;amp; External Affairs&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;21000 - Presidents Office&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$171,737, plus university issued vehicle.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 96px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 96px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 96px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/admin.htm\"&gt;Admin / Admin Temp Benefit Plans&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 96px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;N/A&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;At Will&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;The Vice President for Governmental Relations &amp;amp; External Affairs provides strategic leadership for the University’s governmental relations, external affairs, and public policy efforts. Reporting to the President, this position serves as the University’s principal liaison with federal, state, and local government officials and agencies and works to advance the University’s mission, priorities, and interests through effective government and community engagement.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Vice President develops and implements comprehensive governmental relations strategies; monitors legislative and regulatory developments; builds and maintains relationships with elected and appointed officials; and represents the University before governmental entities and other external stakeholders. The position works closely with the President, Board of Trustees, senior leaders, faculty, staff, students, and external partners to identify opportunities, assess potential impacts of public policy, and coordinate the University’s response to legislative and regulatory issues.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Vice President also leads efforts to identify and pursue public funding opportunities, including state and federal appropriations, grants, capital projects, and other governmental resources that support the University’s strategic priorities. This position may have a primary work location in both Lansing and Big Rapids.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Vice President, in collaboration with the President, will build strategic relationships with businesses and corporations throughout Michigan, with a particular focus on Southeast and West Michigan. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Offers are determined based on a review of the candidate's qualifications, including education, training, experience, and internal pay equity considerations. &lt;br&gt;Placement within the range will generally be based on the following factors:&lt;br&gt;Entry-Range: Candidates who meet the minimum qualifications and core requirements of the position.&lt;br&gt;Mid-Range: Candidates with three or more years of directly related professional experience and demonstrate proficiency in the key responsibilities of the role.&lt;br&gt;Upper Range: Candidates with seven or more years of directly related experience, advanced knowledge, specialized skills, certifications, or expertise that provide significant value to the position.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Final compensation will be determined based on the candidate's overall qualifications, experience, and alignment with the University's compensation philosophy in consultation with Human Resources.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;A Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Significant progressively responsible experience in governmental relations, public policy, legislative&lt;br&gt;affairs, higher education, government, public administration, or a related field.&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated experience developing and implementing governmental or legislative strategies. Demonstrated experience building and maintaining effective relationships with elected officials, government agencies, legislative staff, and other external stakeholders. Excellent written, verbal, interpersonal, presentation, and negotiation skills.&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated ability to analyze complex legislative and regulatory issues and communicate their implications to senior leadership.&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a highly collaborative, politically sensitive, and complex environment.&lt;br&gt;Ability to represent the University effectively with a wide range of internal and external constituencies.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Office Environment&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Balancing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Driving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Develop and execute a comprehensive governmental relations strategy aligned with the University’s strategic plan, institutional priorities, and mission.&lt;br&gt;*Serve as the University’s primary representative and advocate with federal, state, and local elected officials, government agencies, legislative staff, and other governmental stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;*Establish and maintain strong, collaborative relationships with members of the state and federal legislature, local government leaders, and their staffs.&lt;br&gt;*Monitor federal, state, and local legislation, regulations, policies, and governmental actions that may affect the University, higher education, students, employees, or the communities the University serves.&lt;br&gt;*Advise the President, Board of Trustees, and senior leadership regarding legislative and public policy developments, emerging issues, risks, and opportunities.&lt;br&gt;*Develop strategies and recommendations for advancing the University’s legislative and public policy priorities.&lt;br&gt;*Coordinate the University’s response to proposed legislation, regulations, and governmental initiatives in collaboration with appropriate University leaders and subject matter experts.&lt;br&gt;*Represent the University at legislative hearings, governmental meetings, policy forums, community events, and other external engagements.&lt;br&gt;*Develop and maintain relationships with higher education associations, business and community organizations, advocacy groups, and other strategic partners to advance shared priorities.&lt;br&gt;*Coordinate the development and delivery of legislative testimony, briefing materials, policy statements, talking points, correspondence, presentations, and other governmental relations communications.&lt;br&gt;*Identify and pursue opportunities for state and federal appropriations, capital funding, grants, and other public resources that support University priorities.&lt;br&gt;*Work collaboratively with University leadership to develop funding requests and advocacy strategies for capital projects, academic programs, student initiatives, research, workforce development, and other institutional priorities.&lt;br&gt;*Coordinate governmental relations activities across the University to ensure consistent messaging, effective advocacy, and appropriate engagement with public officials.&lt;br&gt;*Serve as a resource to University leaders regarding governmental processes, legislative strategy, public policy, and political and regulatory developments.&lt;br&gt;*Develop and maintain an effective network of governmental and community contacts throughout the University’s service area and beyond.&lt;br&gt;*Promote the University’s contributions to economic development, workforce development, research, innovation, community engagement, and the broader public good.&lt;br&gt;*Collaborate with Communications and Marketing to ensure governmental relations messaging is consistent with the University’s overall communications strategy.&lt;br&gt;*Ensure governmental relations activities comply with applicable federal and state laws, University policies, and ethical standards. Represent the University with professionalism, integrity, and diplomacy while maintaining appropriate political and institutional relationships.&lt;br&gt;*Create partnerships within the community to provide student experiences with governmental agencies. Manage the governmental relations budget and related external consulting or advocacy resources.&lt;br&gt;*Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties.&lt;br&gt;*Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;*Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically.&lt;br&gt;*Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives.&lt;br&gt;*Perform other duties as assigned by the President.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ability to: communicate effectively, including public speaking; influence policymakers; interact effectively with a wide variety of people and groups; plan, organize, and meet deadlines; and be creative and innovative in the development of ideas.&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;br&gt;The position requires the ability to build consensus, navigate complex political and institutional environments, and effectively represent the University’s interests while maintaining productive relationships with individuals and organizations holding differing perspectives.&lt;br&gt;The Vice President is expected to demonstrate sound judgment, political awareness, discretion, and a strong understanding of the role of public higher education within state and federal governmental systems.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of unofficial transcript of Bachelor's degree. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Finalist will be required to submit an official transcript.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;October 5, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498197&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Administrative,Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>B - Executive</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498198</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498198</link><title>Assistant Director of Residential Programs and Services</title><description>Provide primary responsibility for the administration of the Residence Halls, Apartments, and Suites on campus.  Provide leadership and supervision for residential programs and services.  Assist in the development and implementation of comprehensive policies and procedures for on-campus housing operations. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future.  The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Required: Bachelor’s degree in personnel administration, counseling, or related field. 3-5 years of work experience in University housing and residence life with responsibilities which involved supervision (student or professional), corrective action, conflict resolution, and programming in a University setting.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Administrative,Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498198</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 770px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Assistant Director of Residential Programs and Services&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;62102 - Housing and Residence Life&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$57,445&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 96px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 96px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 96px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/admin.htm\"&gt;Admin / Admin Temp Benefit Plans&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 96px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;N/A&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;At Will&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Provide primary responsibility for the administration of the Residence Halls, Apartments, and Suites on campus. Provide leadership and supervision for residential programs and services. Assist in the development and implementation of comprehensive policies and procedures for on-campus housing operations.&lt;br&gt;The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Bachelor’s degree in personnel administration, counseling, or related field.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;3-5 years of work experience in University housing and residence life with responsibilities which involved supervision (student or professional), corrective action, conflict resolution, and programming in a University setting.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 137px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 137px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 137px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Office Environment&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Driving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 137px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Master’s degree in student affairs leadership or related field&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Provide leadership of the residence hall, apartment, and suite system.&lt;br&gt;• Recommend for hire, train, and supervise approximately seven full-time, professional hall and community director staff.&lt;br&gt;• Guide selection, training, and supervision of approximately 100 student hall staff, including Resident Advisors (RA), Community Advisors (CA), and Senior Staff Advisors (SSA), as well as approximately 50-60 Desk Services Assistants (DSA).&lt;br&gt;• Develop and implement processes for effective response to crisis situations.&lt;br&gt;• Facilitate and participate in on-call rotation for crisis management. &lt;br&gt;• Provide supervision for desk operations in approximately 13 on-campus living communities. &lt;br&gt;• Direct professional staff recruitment initiatives.&lt;br&gt;• Coordinate Hall and Community Director involvement in support of other department/division operations and programs.&lt;br&gt;• Advise the Residence Hall Association (RHA) student organization, which leads programming for and represents on-campus residents.&lt;br&gt;• Coordinate assessment initiatives for the department. &lt;br&gt;• Provide guidance for residence hall staff and students.&lt;br&gt;• Serve as a referral agent to ensure student needs are met.&lt;br&gt;• Develop and maintain RA Resource area and materials. &lt;br&gt;• Serve as a liaison to other offices, including the Office of Student Conduct. &lt;br&gt;• Develop, maintain, and supervise budget standards for individual residence hall operations. &lt;br&gt;• Serve as first appeal for off-campus requests, staff discipline, and student employment issues.&lt;br&gt;• Visit and inspect all on-campus living areas, monitor programming efforts, and facilitate staff meetings.&lt;br&gt;• Represent the department on special committees and meetings &lt;br&gt;• Assist with central office management. &lt;br&gt;• Assist with operations management, facilities management, enrollment initiatives, and marketing. &lt;br&gt;• Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. &lt;br&gt;• Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;• Train and supervise professional and student staff on safety and emergency procedures, crisis response, mandated reporting responsibilities, incident report writing, community building, programming, and other university processes and functions to ensure the building of a highly responsive, compassionate, and responsible on-campus living environment for approximately 3,400 student residents.&lt;br&gt;• Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;• Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;• Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;• Serve on University committees.&lt;br&gt;• Attend meetings, workshops, and conferences in absence of supervisor&lt;br&gt;• Assist in the ongoing revision and development of internal and external communications&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Understand student development theory.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrate communication skills, including the ability to speak to large groups.&lt;br&gt;• Work collaboratively with other University and community constituencies.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated ability to supervise and lead a diverse group of students and staff. &lt;br&gt;• Mediate conflict successfully.&lt;br&gt;• Use basic computer programs.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;Unofficial Transcript 2&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of their bachelor's degree. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Unofficial Transcript 2 (OPTIONAL): Applicants who have attained a Master’s degree in student affairs leadership or related field please attach a copy of unofficial transcript.&lt;br&gt;Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Finalist will be required to submit an official transcript&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 28, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498198&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Administrative,Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>E - Student Affairs</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498199</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498199</link><title>LGBTQ+ Resource Student Asst (Student Position)</title><description>The LGBTQ+ resource center is seeking a student assistant. In this position, you will greet students and offer them resources.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - Work Study Only</job:category><job:refNo>498199</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 106.761%; height: 236px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;LGBTQ+ Resource Center Student Assistant (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;LGBTQ+ Resource Center&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00 - $14.49&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;The LGBTQ+ resource center is seeking a student assistant. In this position, you will greet students and offer them resources.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Please use the \"Other Additional Document\" section to submit a letter of interest for why you want to work at the LGBTQ+ Resource Center, and any specific and relevant experiences you would like to highlight that would make you a good fit for the role.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Greet students and assist them with accessing the resources that the LGBTQ+ resource center offers&lt;br&gt;*Be a point of contact for students visiting the center when the LGBTQ+ program coordinator is not available&lt;br&gt;*Assist with the design and implementation of programs hosted by the center&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule, Letter of Interest&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;November 1, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498199&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Mon, 02 Nov 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - Work Study Only</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - Work Study Only</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>I - Diversity, Incl &amp; Strat Initiatives</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498200</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498200</link><title>Adjunct Instructor - Writing Center Specialist (Part Time)</title><description>Writing Center Specialists provide writing consultation (on-site and electronic/digital) to undergraduate and graduate students for 10 to 28 hours per week. The successful applicant will be familiar with APA and MLA documentation and must be comfortable working one-on-one with a diverse student population representing a full range of majors and writing skills, from remedial to advanced. The successful applicant must be comfortable working in face-to-face and electronic/digital instructional settings. This is a pooled position. One or more applicants may be hired to assist students on a semester-by-semester basis. The anticipated start date of this position will be throughout the academic year, with some initial appointments in September 2026. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc. Required: Bachelor’s degree in English, English Education, History, Social Sciences, or a related field. One year of experience involving tutoring and teaching at the K-12 and/or college level. Experience working with diverse populations, including ESL.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Faculty</job:category><job:refNo>498200</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 715px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Adjunct Instructor - Writing Center Specialist (Part Time)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;33203 - Writing Center&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$19.96 per hour pursuant to the FSU and FNTFO/AFT Letter of Agreement&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 96px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 96px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 96px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/adjunct.htm\"&gt;Adjunct Faculty&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 96px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Ferris Nontenure-Track Faculty Organization (FNTFO) (AFT)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;9 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Writing Center Specialists provide writing consultation (on-site and electronic/digital) to undergraduate and graduate students for 10 to 28 hours per week. The successful applicant will be familiar with APA and MLA documentation and must be comfortable working one-on-one with a diverse student population representing a full range of majors and writing skills, from remedial to advanced. The successful applicant must be comfortable working in face-to-face and electronic/digital instructional settings.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a pooled position. One or more applicants may be hired to assist students on a semester-by-semester basis. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The anticipated start date of this position will be throughout the academic year, with some initial appointments in September 2026.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H1B, etc.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Faculty - Temporary &amp;amp; Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Bachelor's degree in English, English Education, History, Social Sciences, or a related field.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;One year of experience involving tutoring and/or teaching at the K-12 and/or college level.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Experience working with diverse student populations, including ESL.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 82px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 82px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 82px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Office Environment&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 82px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;This position requires providing writing consultation (both on-site and electronic/digital) to undergraduate and graduate students. The successful applicant will be familiar with APA and MLA documentation and must be comfortable working one-on-one with a diverse student population representing a full range of majors and writing skills.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Schedule appointments that meet students' needs. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train/mentor other writing center specialists.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Coordinate writing workshops with assistance of the director. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Provide input to the specialists' team and director on innovative tutoring/teaching methods/modalities. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep abreast of current writing center theory and practice. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivate an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of Bachelor's degree. Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498200&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Faculty - Temporary &amp; Continuing</job:workType><job:category>Faculty</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498203</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498203</link><title>Food Service Worker</title><description>A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at Erbert &amp; Gerbert's. The normal working hours are 5:00 a.m. to 1:30 p.m., Sunday through Thursday. Days off are Friday and Saturday. The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498203</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Food Service Worker&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;51800 - Dining Overhead&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.53 - Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;9 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at Erbert &amp;amp; Gerbert's. &lt;br&gt;• The normal working hours are 5:00 a.m. to 1:30 p.m., Sunday through Thursday. &lt;br&gt;• Days off are Friday and Saturday. &lt;br&gt;• The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. &lt;br&gt;• If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. &lt;br&gt;• Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. &lt;br&gt;• Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Electrical Hazards&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Balancing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Train others in the performance of the characteristic duties as directed.&lt;br&gt;• Assist other food service employees as needed.&lt;br&gt;• Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives.&lt;br&gt;• Assure that food is palatable and appetizing.&lt;br&gt;• Cook and handle food according to safe food handling/sanitary requirements following departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;• Interact with customers and staff in a polite, friendly, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain equipment, pots, pans, utensils, and work area in a clean, orderly, and sanitary condition following departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;• Minimize food waste.&lt;br&gt;• Obtain foods from storage areas.&lt;br&gt;• Operate various kitchen equipment, machines, and utilize utensils.&lt;br&gt;• Perform the work of other Dining Service classifications when assigned.&lt;br&gt;• Prepare food for serving and assure continued food availability.&lt;br&gt;• Prepare foods using recipes generated from the computerized menu management system.&lt;br&gt;• Respond to special dietary requests.&lt;br&gt;• Set up and maintain food preparation area, food serving, and display areas, in an attractive and sanitary manner.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain safety and sanitation standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;• Report to immediate supervisor and/or designee.&lt;br&gt;• Train and guide the work of student employees in the performance of the characteristic duties. &lt;br&gt;• Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;• Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;• Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;• Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;• Remove trash, break down cardboard boxes, and assist in the University recycling efforts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Ability to communicate effectively.&lt;br&gt;• Ability to interact with the public in a friendly, polite, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;• Experience working directly with people from diverse racial, ethnic, and socioeconomic backgrounds.&lt;br&gt;• Be familiar with seasoning requirements and kitchen equipment.&lt;br&gt;• Cook a variety of foods in large and small quantities.&lt;br&gt;• Follow safety and sanitation standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;• Keep accurate records.&lt;br&gt;• Read, understand, and follow recipes, directions, safety labels, equipment operations manuals, etc.&lt;br&gt;• Work harmoniously with others in variable temperatures, close confines, noise, stressful situations, and workloads.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498203&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498205</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498205</link><title>Food Service Worker</title><description>A Food Service Worker position is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 6:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m. Sunday through Thursday. Days off are Friday and Saturday.  However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position.  NOTE: Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498205</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Food Service Worker&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;51804 - The Rock Cafe&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.53. Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;A Food Service Worker position is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 6:00 a.m. to 2:30 p.m. Sunday through Thursday. Days off are Friday and Saturday. However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position. NOTE: Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Balancing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;As directed, train others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assist other food service employees as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assure that food is palatable and appetizing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook and handle food in accordance with safe food-handling and sanitary requirements, following departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interact with customers and staff in a polite, friendly, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain equipment, pots, pans, utensils, and the work area in a clean, orderly, and sanitary condition, in accordance with departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimize food waste.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Obtain foods from storage areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate various kitchen equipment and machines, utilize utensils.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Perform the work of other Dining Service classifications when assigned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare food for service and ensure continued availability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare foods using recipes generated from the computerized menu management system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respond to special dietary requests.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set up and maintain food preparation, serving, and display areas in an attractive and sanitary manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Other duties may be assigned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and sanitation standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report to immediate supervisor and/or designee.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train and direct the work of student employees in performing the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Remove trash, break down cardboard boxes, and assist in the University recycling efforts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ability to communicate effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ability to interact with the public in a friendly, polite, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be familiar with seasoning requirements and kitchen equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook a variety of foods in large and small quantities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Follow safety and sanitation standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep accurate records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow recipes, directions, safety labels, equipment operations manuals, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work harmoniously with others in variable temperatures, close confines, noise, and stressful situations and workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498205&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498207</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498207</link><title>Temporary Food Service Worker</title><description>A position classified as a Temporary Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 6 a.m. - 2:30 pm, Tuesday through Saturday.  Days off are Sunday and Monday.  The exact duration of this temporary position is undetermined at this time, but it will not exceed one year.  This position will begin on September 15, or sooner, subject to approval. However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498207</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Temporary Food Service Worker&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;51804 - The Rock Cafe&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.53. Hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Temporary&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;A position classified as a Temporary Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 6 a.m. - 2:30 pm, Tuesday through Saturday. Days off are Sunday and Monday. The exact duration of this temporary position is undetermined at this time, but it will not exceed one year. This position will begin on September 15, or sooner, subject to approval. However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, the employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Balancing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Provide food service support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining the assigned area.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As directed, train others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assist other food service employees as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assure that food is palatable and appetizing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook and handle food in accordance with safe food-handling and sanitary requirements, following departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interact with customers and staff in a polite, friendly, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain equipment, pots, pans, utensils, and the work area in a clean, orderly, and sanitary condition in accordance with departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimize food waste.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Obtain foods from storage areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate various kitchen equipment and machines, utilize utensils.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Perform the work of other Dining Service classifications when assigned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare food for service and ensure continued availability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare foods using recipes generated from the computerized menu management system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respond to special dietary requests.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set up and maintain food preparation, serving, and display areas in an attractive and sanitary manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and sanitation standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report to immediate supervisor and/or designee.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train and direct the work of student employees in performing the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Remove trash, break down cardboard boxes, and assist in the University recycling efforts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ability to communicate effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ability to interact with the public in a friendly, polite, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be familiar with seasoning requirements and kitchen equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook a variety of foods in large and small quantities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Follow safety and sanitation standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep accurate records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow recipes, directions, safety labels, equipment operations manuals, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work harmoniously with others in variable temperatures, close confines, noise, and stressful situations and workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498207&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498209</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498209</link><title>Temporary Food Service Worker</title><description>A position classified as a Temporary Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Café. The normal working hours are 1:30pm-10:00pm Sunday, Monday and Thursday through Saturday.  Days off are Tuesday and Wednesday. The exact duration of this temporary position is undetermined at this time.  The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends.  If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498209</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Temporary Food Service Worker&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;51804 - The Rock Cafe&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.53- hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Temporary&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;A position classified as a Temporary Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Café. The normal working hours are 1:30pm-10:00pm Sunday, Monday and Thursday through Saturday. Days off are Tuesday and Wednesday. The exact duration of this temporary position is undetermined at this time. The employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. This is an AFSCME bargaining unit position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Balancing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;As directed, train others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assist other food service employees as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assure that food is palatable and appetizing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook and handle food in accordance with safe food-handling and sanitary requirements, following departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interact with customers and staff in a polite, friendly, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain equipment, pots, pans, utensils, and the work area in a clean, orderly, and sanitary condition, in accordance with departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimize food waste.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Obtain foods from storage areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate various kitchen equipment and machines, utilize utensils.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Perform the work of other Dining Service classifications when assigned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare food for service and ensure continued availability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare foods using recipes generated from the computerized menu management system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respond to special dietary requests.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set up and maintain food preparation, food serving, and display areas in an attractive and sanitary manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and sanitation standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report to immediate supervisor and/or designee.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train and direct the work of student employees in performing the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;Carry out these responsibilities in accordance with University policies and applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Remove trash, break down cardboard boxes, and assist in the University recycling efforts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ability to communicate effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ability to interact with the public in a friendly, polite, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be familiar with seasoning requirements and kitchen equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook a variety of foods in large and small quantities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Follow safety and sanitation standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep accurate records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow recipes, directions, safety labels, equipment operations manuals, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work harmoniously with others in variable temperatures; close confines; noise and stressful situations and workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498209&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498210</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498210</link><title>Part-Time Bus Driver</title><description>Provide safe transportation for passengers, equipment, and packages. Assist in maintenance of University owned and leased vehicles. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Valid Michigan commercial driver’s license (CDL), Group A or B with endorsements ‘P’ with no restrictions, airbrakes and DOT medical card. Three years full-time equivalent of combined bus and heavy equipment truck driving, with emphasis on bus driving experience. Demonstrated experience with minor automotive repair and driving all types of vehicles.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff,Part-Time</job:category><job:refNo>498210</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part-Time Bus Driver&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;55301 - Transportation Services&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$22.00&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/parttime.htm\"&gt;Part Time Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;N/A&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;As Needed&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Provide safe transportation for passengers, equipment, and packages. Assist in maintenance of University owned and leased vehicles.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Three years full-time equivalent of combined bus and heavy equipment truck driving, with emphasis on bus driving experience. Demonstrated experience with minor automotive repair and driving all types of vehicles.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Valid Michigan commercial driver’s license (CDL), Group A or B with endorsements ‘P’ with no restrictions, airbrakes and DOT medical card.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Inclement Weather&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Driving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Check the safety of lights, tires, water, battery, fluids (windshield washer, oil, power steering), and replace or add as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Clean and/or deliver a variety of goods and equipment to/from off- and on-campus locations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Drive commercial-type vehicles to safely transport students, faculty, and/or add as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Pick up/deliveries to/from campus, newly purchased University vehicles, and pick up, haul, and/or deliver a variety of goods and equipment to/from off- and on-campus locations.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report needed repairs that warrant mechanic’s attention.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wash, vacuum, and extract the motor vehicle interior and/or as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and health standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report to immediate supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Assist other service workers as needed.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Available to work days, evenings, and weekends.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Check and correct the safety of vehicle lights and fluid levels.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Communicate effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep accurate records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow directions. Check and correct the safety of vehicle lights and fluid levels.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Understand, use good judgment, and follow procedures established through safety training and the physical plant safety manual.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work harmoniously with others in situations with variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work independently.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Meet applicable Department of Transportation requirements.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Must pass physical exam and drug test every two years.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Test drug free and/or to submitting application.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498210&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff,Part-Time</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498211</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498211</link><title>Part Time Temporary Personal Counselor</title><description>This is a temporary, part time clinical position. The position will provide individual and group short-term mental health counseling and crisis intervention for Ferris State University (FSU) students. This position will end following the fall semester (December 11, 2026) This position may not work more than 28 hours per week. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F1 EAD’s, OPT, H1B, etc.. Required: Master's Degree in Professional Counseling, and/or Counseling Psychology, and/or Clinical Psychology, and/or Social Work, and/or Marriage and Family Therapy and/or comparable mental health professional degree. Active license (or application for license pending) to practice in the state of Michigan, LMSW and/or LLP and/or LPC and/or LP, TLLP or LLPC, LLMSW. Demonstrated experience in counseling clients with a wide range of psychological and emotional health concerns.</description><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff,Part-Time</job:category><job:refNo>498211</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part Time Temporary Personal Counselor&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;62901 - Personal Counseling Center&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13,720.00&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/parttime.htm\"&gt;Part Time Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Temporary&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;N/A&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Less than 9 month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;This is a temporary, part time clinical position. The position will provide individual and group short-term mental health counseling and crisis intervention for Ferris State University (FSU) students. This position will end following the fall semester (December 11, 2026) This position may not work more than 28 hours per week.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F1 EAD’s, OPT, H1B, etc.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Master's Degree in Professional Counseling, and/or Counseling Psychology, and/or Clinical Psychology, and/or Social Work, and/or Marriage and Family Therapy and/or comparable mental health professional degree&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Demonstrated experience in counseling clients with a wide range of psychological and emotional health concerns&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Active license (or application for license pending) to practice in the state of Michigan, LMSW and/or LLP and/or LPC and/or LP, TLLP or LLPC, LLMSW&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Office Environment&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;One year of experience providing mental health therapy preferred. Experience working in a college or university counseling center preferred.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Provide short-term individual, couple, or group counseling to a diverse student body using empirically based treatment methods and accepted standards of practice within one's professional discipline.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Provide crisis intervention, risk assessments, and safety plans for students identified as a risk to themselves or others on an as-needed basis. This will include partnering with various campus departments in handling mental health emergencies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain high-quality care coordination for clients, including adequate referrals for evaluation or treatment, communicating with involved treatment providers, supporting family members when appropriate, tracking students of concern, and maintaining appropriate and timely confidential client records in an electronic record system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Directly report to the Director of the Personal Counseling Center.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Responsible for maintaining professional competence and license(s) by continuing relevant professional training and development in best practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of designated protected information and performing duties in compliance with applicable policies, procedures, legal mandates, and code of ethics.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Participates in all other duties as requested and/or assigned by the Director.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Provides support staff functions and coverage in the absence of support staff with the other counselors.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Must be able to work in a team-oriented atmosphere as a partner within the department as well as the campus community.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Must be comfortable with computer software applications, such as Microsoft Office Suite, and navigating an electronic medical records system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Must have excellent communication skills, both oral and written.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Certification/License&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of unofficial transcript of Master's Degree in Professional Counseling, and/or Counseling Psychology, and/or Clinical Psychology, and/or Social Work, and/or Marriage and Family Therapy and/or comparable mental health professional degree.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Transcript must include: Institution name, applicant name, date degree attained, degree awarded. Finalist will be required to submit an official transcript.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;License (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of active license (or application for license pending) to practice in the state of Michigan, LMSW and/or LLP and/or LPC and/or LP, TLLP or LLPC, LLMSW.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 21, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498211&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff,Part-Time</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>E - Student Affairs</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498195</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498195</link><title>Torch Freelance Reporter (Student Position)</title><description>The Torch is looking for a freelance porter. This position may be your opportunity to use your skills as well as gain further experience.</description><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-02T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498195</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Torch Freelance Reporter (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;College of Arts and Sciences&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73- $13.99&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;The Torch is looking for a freelance porter. This position may be your opportunity to use your skills as well as gain further experience.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Researching a story&lt;br&gt;*Obtaining the facts&lt;br&gt;*Providing photographs or video&lt;br&gt;*Conducting interviews&lt;br&gt;*Writing the story&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;14&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498195&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498194</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498194</link><title>CAPS Clerical 1 (Student Position)</title><description>Want to get exposed to everything that Ferris State has to offer? Career and Professional Success! You will get to help out at many events across campus, create advertisements, and other clerical duties.</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-09-01T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - Work Study Only</job:category><job:refNo>498194</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 236px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;CAPS Clerical 1 (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;CAPS&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73-$13.99&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Want to get exposed to everything that Ferris State has to offer? Career and Professional Success! You will get to help out at many events across campus, create advertisements, and other clerical duties.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;- Compassion and interest in working with students, faculty, staff, and employers&lt;br&gt;- Some understanding of Ferris structures and resources &lt;br&gt;- Attention to detail&lt;br&gt;- Some technology proficiency with Microsoft products and Canva&lt;br&gt;- Must have a 2.5 GPA&lt;br&gt;- Must be able to pass a background check by the university&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;- Participate in regular staff meetings&lt;br&gt;- Assist professional staff with clerical tasks which may include: scheduling meetings, returning phone calls, answering emails, taking meeting minutes, purchasing items, and proofreading documents.&lt;br&gt;- Assist at events&lt;br&gt;- Create advertising posters&lt;br&gt;- Advertise CAPS events&lt;br&gt;- Provide feedback and suggestions for innovative changes &lt;br&gt;- Plan, implement, and evaluate programming - Including but not limited to room reservations, catering reservations, advertising, supply purchases, cash handling, event set-up, staffing events, and finding and leading volunteers. &lt;br&gt;- Other duties as assigned.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;September 18, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498194&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 03:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - Work Study Only</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - Work Study Only</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>E - Student Affairs</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498191</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498191</link><title>Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position)</title><description>Support daily operations of School of Digital Media labs—enforcing lab rules, maintaining equipment, managing seat reservations/usage—and assist in other program‑specific tasks.\n\nDAGD Lab: Advising students on software operation. Guiding, advising and consulting on projects. Maintaining order in the labs.\nEsports Lab: Assisting production and content team to create media for social media and broadcasts.</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-31T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498191</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Esports and Digital Lab Monitor (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;School of Digital Media&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Support daily operations of School of Digital Media labs—enforcing lab rules, maintaining equipment, managing seat reservations/usage—and assist in other program‑specific tasks.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;DAGD Lab: Advising students on software operation. Guiding, advising and consulting on projects. Maintaining order in the labs.&lt;br&gt;Esports Lab: Assisting production and content team to create media for social media and broadcasts.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Student Position&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Familiarity with the rules, practices, and workflows of collegiate digital media labs such as esports or Digital Animation and Game Design (DAGD)&lt;br&gt;• Basic computer‑hardware and software troubleshooting skills&lt;br&gt;• Excellent customer service and communication skills&lt;br&gt;• Strong attention to detail&lt;br&gt;• Some understanding of Ferris State University structures and resources&lt;br&gt;• Availability to work scheduled shifts from Esports Lab Hours - 4&amp;nbsp;PM–12&amp;nbsp;AM on weekdays and 12&amp;nbsp;PM–12&amp;nbsp;AM on weekends; DAGD Lab Hours - 8 PM–12 AM on weekdays and 2pm-10PM weekends.&lt;br&gt;• Preferred interest in content production and digital media; experience with social‑media and content‑creation software (Adobe Creative Suite – Photoshop, Lightroom, Premiere, After Effects – and/or DaVinci Resolve)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;• Greet and assist all participants and visitors in the labs, enforcing lab rules and safety protocols&lt;br&gt;• Monitor, maintain, and troubleshoot hardware, peripherals, and workstations&lt;br&gt;• Manage seat reservations, check‑in procedures, and track lab usage statistics&lt;br&gt;• Maintain cleanliness and organization of the lab and equipment storage areas&lt;br&gt;• Support event setup, staffing, and breakdown for program activities&lt;br&gt;• Attend regular team meetings and contribute ideas for improving lab operations and strategies&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Other Duties May Include:&lt;br&gt;• Capture and edit game clips/highlights; produce graphics and short‑form videos for social platforms (Twitter, Instagram, TikTok, YouTube)&lt;br&gt;• Assist with live broadcast production, including camera setup, scene transitions, and overlay management&lt;br&gt;• Coordinate with production teams to resolve audiovisual issues during streams or media projects&lt;br&gt;• Assist with content creation, media production, or other program‑specific projects for esports, Digital Animation and Game Design (DAGD), or related disciplines&lt;br&gt;• Other duties as assigned&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Resume, Class Schedule&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please include a sample of your content work (e.g., link to portfolio or social media channels). Be prepared to provide your weekly availability schedule when contacted for an interview.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498191&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498173</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498173</link><title>Assistant Professor - Economics (9 Mos Tenure Track)</title><description>The College of Business at Ferris State University seeks a diverse group of outstanding applicants for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Economics. Teaching will include economics undergraduate and graduate courses. Candidates are expected to foster a meaningful learning experience for our students; faculty are expected to be student-oriented, advise, and integrate current technology into the learning environment. Additionally, faculty will participate in collaborative efforts to advance curricular initiatives, participate in the assessment of student learning, and further develop programmatic enhancements. Specifically, we expect the candidate to be willing to engage students outside the classroom, support and expand our existing academic initiatives, and mentor students beyond a traditional academic advising role. In support of teaching, faculty will engage in scholarly/professional activities and participate in department, college, and university committees. The selected candidate should be willing to serve as a program coordinator. Off-campus and online teaching may be required. Courses are to be taught in person on one of Ferris State University's Campuses or online. The candidate selected for the position must reside in Michigan after acceptance of employment and will perform duties at a Ferris site. The anticipated start date of this position is January 2027 at the earliest and August 2027 at the latest. The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H-1 B, etc.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Faculty</job:category><job:refNo>498173</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Assistant Professor - Economics (9 Mos Tenure Track)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;34400 - Management&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$107,000 - $112,000; Salary commensurate with education, experience, and other requirements.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/faculty.htm\"&gt;Faculty Health Benefit Plans&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Ferris Faculty Association (MEA-NEA)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;9 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;The College of Business at Ferris State University seeks a diverse group of outstanding applicants for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor position in the Department of Economics. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Teaching will include economics undergraduate and graduate courses. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Candidates are expected to foster a meaningful learning experience for our students; faculty are expected to be student-oriented, advise, and integrate current technology into the learning environment. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Additionally, faculty will participate in collaborative efforts to advance curricular initiatives, participate in the assessment of student learning, and further develop programmatic enhancements. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Specifically, we expect the candidate to be willing to engage students outside the classroom, support and expand our existing academic initiatives, and mentor students beyond a traditional academic advising role. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;In support of teaching, faculty will engage in scholarly/professional activities and participate in department, college, and university committees. The selected candidate should be willing to serve as a program coordinator. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Off-campus and online teaching may be required. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Courses are to be taught in person on one of Ferris State University's Campuses or online. The candidate selected for the position must reside in Michigan after acceptance of employment and will perform duties at a Ferris site. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The anticipated start date of this position is January 2027 at the earliest and August 2027 at the latest.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The selected candidate for this position must be authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire without employer assistance or sponsorship now or in the future. The university will not assist with any F-1 EADs, OPT, H-1 B, etc.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Faculty - Temporary &amp;amp; Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Doctorate (Ph.D.) in Economics (ABD may be considered if the candidate has substantial progress toward degree completion).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Evidence of teaching excellence at a university level, particularly in relation to economics; the ability to effectively merge economic theory and practice; excellent interpersonal and communications skills, and evidence of teaching excellence in a face to face environment.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Office Environment&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Prepared to teach courses in Austrian Economics, Economic Development, Health Economics, and Law and Economics . &lt;br&gt;Prior university-level teaching experience in economics. &lt;br&gt;Evidence of ongoing scholarship/publication or other professional activity.&lt;br&gt;Experience with active learning, data-driven instruction, and technology-enhanced teaching.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Primary teaching responsibilities include: Teaching Principles of Microeconomics and Principles of Macroeconomics. Teaching advanced economics electives and/or graduate-level courses as assigned based on departmental need and candidate qualifications. Supporting a meaningful learning experience by: being student-orientated, advising students, and integrating current technology into the learning environments.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Teaching will generally fall within the umbrella of principles of economics courses, however advanced courses including graduate may be assigned. To foster a meaningful learning experience for our students, faculty are expected to be student-oriented, to advise, to integrate current technology into the learning environment, and to enjoy participating in collaborative efforts to foster curricular and programmatic enhancement. In support of teaching, they will engage in scholarly/professional activities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Faculty members also have professional responsibilities which may include advising students, orientation and registration of students, participation in university committees, keeping regular posted office hours (which are scheduled at times convenient for students), and participation in traditional functions which have academic significance (e.g.) reporting initial student participation data and submitting final grades on time).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Faculty members may be required to teach off-campus or in and online environment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Teach full-time during the 9-month academic year (or 12 month).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Recruitment of students (including Dawg Days, Admitted Student Days, visits to high schools or career tech centers, and other University-outreach events) will occur throughout the academic year and include some Saturdays.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Serve on program committees and represent the program(s) on College and University committees.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Collaborate with faculty on curriculum development, assessment, and quality assurance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Candidates are expected to teach at both the Big Rapids and/or Grand Rapids campuses.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Teach and coordinate elective courses in areas of expertise.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Collaborate in design and implementation of additional undergraduate and graduate degrees.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain records and conduct assessment and advising in accordance with policies and procedures developed by the university, college, school, department, and/or program.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Perform duties in accordance with established University policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Act as liaison between the program and professional organizations through active, individual involvement and, potentially as the program-appointed representative.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Enthusiastically support student success through active involvement with individual students, student organizations, and student competitions, both within and outside of the classroom.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Remain current in the profession.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The position reports to the Department Chair or Director and the Dean.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ferris State University's philosophy places excellence in teaching as the first priority while encouraging involvements in scholarly activity.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work with colleagues to develop new curricular initiatives.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1 (REQUIRED): Applicants must attach a copy of an unofficial transcript of their Doctoral degree. &lt;br&gt;Transcripts must include the institution name, the applicant's name, the date the degree was attained, and the degree awarded. Finalists will be required to submit an official transcript.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 28, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498173&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Faculty - Temporary &amp; Continuing</job:workType><job:category>Faculty</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498174</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498174</link><title>Dispatch Specialist</title><description>Coordinate the Public Safety Department communication system and perform a variety of police records support functions, some of which require special certification. This position will be expected to work different/longer hours during times of emergency. This is a CTA-MEA/NEA position. Required: Associate’s Degree. LEIN certified or achieve such certification within 60 days of hire. Six months work experience in dispatching, law enforcement, or as an equivalent emergency communication professional.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff,Clerical</job:category><job:refNo>498174</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Dispatch Specialist&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;57000 - Public Safety&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$23.43 hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and CTA/MEA-NEA Agreement&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/cta.htm\"&gt;Clerical Tech Association (CTA)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Clerical-Technical Association (MEA-NEA)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Coordinate the Public Safety Department communication system and perform a variety of police records support functions, some of which require special certification.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This position will be expected to work different/longer hours during times of emergency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a CTA-MEA/NEA position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Associate's Degree&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Six months work experience in dispatching, law enforcement, or as an equivalent emergency communication professional.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;LEIN certified or achieve such certification within 60 days of hire.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Office Environment&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Bachelor's Degree&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;One year of police dispatcher experience.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Formal training in law enforcement and/or dispatching-related discipline.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Answer incoming calls and direct communications to the proper destination and/or assign the appropriate response service such as dispatching police officers to non-emergency complaints, referral of emergency police, fire, and EMS requests to Central Dispatch.&lt;br&gt;• Coordinate police response and services to University students, faculty, and staff as needed.&lt;br&gt;• Monitor and coordinate response to intrusion, hold-up, and fire alarm systems.&lt;br&gt;• Type, keyboard, input, record and file records according to established procedures.&lt;br&gt;• Responsible for the selection, training, scheduling, and supervision of all student dispatchers.&lt;br&gt;• Process payroll for all DPS student employees.&lt;br&gt;• Upon authorization to do so, will initiate and notify constituents via emergency mass communication system in various emergencies.&lt;br&gt;• Serve as active member of the Emergency Response Team (ERT) and assume responsibilities as outlined in the Emergency Response Plan and Procedures.&lt;br&gt;• Review forms and other documents to assure proper completion.&lt;br&gt;• Retrieve and input data utilizing a computer and printer.&lt;br&gt;• Collect fines and fees and issue receipts; issue guest parking permits, and assist in the administration of the parking program as directed.&lt;br&gt;• Validate and edit police reports.&lt;br&gt;• Disseminate police reports/warrant requests.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain supplemental reports.&lt;br&gt;• Certified LEIN operator.&lt;br&gt;• Process abandoned vehicle reports.&lt;br&gt;• Process traffic citations.&lt;br&gt;• Process property dispositions.&lt;br&gt;• Assist General Counsel with FOIA requests.&lt;br&gt;• Conduct background checks for other agencies.&lt;br&gt;• Process requests for police reports.&lt;br&gt;• Conduct driving records checks for Motor Pool and other University departments on an as needed basis.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain confidentiality as required by law and department procedures.&lt;br&gt;• Prepare/coordinate department/University mail/document deliveries.&lt;br&gt;• Responsible for tracking, and appropriately dispatching the Public Safety Officers.&lt;br&gt;• Selection, training and supervising student dispatchers and part-time personnel in dispatch, in accordance with University policies and applicable laws.&lt;br&gt;• Response/coordination of DPS communication in emergencies/mass casualties/disasters.&lt;br&gt;• Serve as the Terminal Agency Coordinator (TAC) as required by the Michigan State Police and FBI CJIC.&lt;br&gt;• Serve as the Local Area Security Officer (LASO) as required by the Michigan State Police and FBI CJIC. &lt;br&gt;• Maintains the department’s records system, as directed.&lt;br&gt;• Report directly to the Director of Public Safety.&lt;br&gt;• Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;• Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;• Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;• Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Register weapons.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Maintain composure in crisis situations and be able to work under the pressure of an emergency situation.&lt;br&gt;• Communicate effectively and be able to successfully interact in unusual situations and with difficult customers.&lt;br&gt;• Use computer software such as word-processing, spreadsheets, database, and other management software.&lt;br&gt;• Successfully interact with visitors, staff, faculty, and students.&lt;br&gt;• Able to share sensitive information on a need-to-know basis only.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Unofficial Transcript 1&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 14, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498174&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff,Clerical</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498176</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498176</link><title>Custodian</title><description>Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. This position is M-F, 5:00 pm - 1:30 am. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Valid driver's license. Custodial/janitorial work experience in a commercial/hospital/school environment in a commercial cleaning service or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498176</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Custodian&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;55200 - Bldg Custodial Admin&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.88 - hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. This position is M-F, 5:00 pm - 1:30 am.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Custodial/janitorial work experience in a commercial/hospital/school environment in a commercial cleaning service or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Valid driver's license&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Electrical Hazards&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Inclement Weather&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Driving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Any other related custodial experience. &lt;br&gt;Please include any/all related work experience associated with the required qualifications for this position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Change linens, make beds, and bunk/debunk beds.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Check the fire extinguisher and related equipment as scheduled, and report any deficiencies to the supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Depending on assignment, may be required to move custodial equipment, fill in for vacant positions, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Disinfect restrooms, showers, and locker rooms.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Empty waste baskets and trash containers, and gather and dispose of trash and foreign material from the assigned area (including the perimeter of the assigned building).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain current knowledge of bloodborne pathogen policies and procedures.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;May be responsible for carrying, distributing, and delivering custodial supplies and equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimize waste of cleaning, paper, soap, and other supplies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Open and close buildings, classrooms, offices, etc. of assigned areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Remove snow and ice from entrances of assigned areas and apply salt as necessary.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Replace light bulbs, globes, tubes, and light lenses.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Replenish paper and soap products.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report needed maintenance on assigned equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report needed repairs to supervisor or call physical plant in emergencies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respond to emergency custodial requests (which could include blood and body fluid clean up).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set up tables, chairs, and other related furniture as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Sweep, wet-mop, refinish hard-surface floors, clean carpet, and vacuum.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Utilize a household plunger to unplug commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wash walls, woodwork, windows, blinds, mirrors, bathroom fixtures, furniture, chalk/white boards, and climb ladders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work with different cleaning chemicals and equipment, and follow procedures for safe handling and use, while wearing assigned protective equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Assist other service workers as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train and guide others in the performance of the characteristic duties. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;Report to immediate supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;May require availability to work other shifts, weekends, and evenings, including overtime and responding to emergency calls.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;If required by job duties, the employee must be able to meet the University's requirements regarding the issuance and use of University keys.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Communicate and work effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Exercise good judgment in resolving situations related to cleaning and proper chemical use, referring unusual problems to the supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain a high standard of cleanliness and follow safety and disinfecting standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow instructions, safety and direction labels, and equipment operation manuals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train and guide others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work harmoniously with and guide others in all situations, including those environments which may involve variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work independently.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Lift supplies and equipment, mop, and empty trash containers and/or bags.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;May be required to work in hot, humid areas and/or cold weather environments and/or to wear personal protective equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;May frequently lift up to 50 lbs. When required to lift, pull, push, etc., heavy objects over 50 pounds, the employee must use good judgment to obtain additional assistance, such as help from a second person or a mechanical device.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate heavy-powered cleaning equipment such as carpet extraction/shampoo equipment, high-speed burnisher, scrubber, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 14, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498176&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498178</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498178</link><title>Custodian</title><description>Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. The anticipated schedule for this position will be Sa-W, 6:00 am – 2:30 pm. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Valid driver's license. Custodial/Janitorial work experience in a commercial-hospital-school environment, in a commercial cleaning service, or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training. Demonstrated experience with correct operation of a variety of commercial custodial equipment such as a vacuum cleaner, automatic scrubber, high-speed burnisher, single-disc scrubber, carpet extraction/shampoo equipment, or other essential or similar custodial equipment.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498178</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Custodian&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;55000 - Physical Plant Admin&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.88 - hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Perform custodial duties independently or within a team environment as assigned, providing a high standard of cleanliness. &lt;br&gt;• The anticipated schedule for this position will be Sa-W, 6:00 am – 2:30 pm.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Custodial/Janitorial work experience in a commercial-hospital-school environment, in a commercial cleaning service, or completion of the Ferris State University JANUS (custodial) training.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated experience with correct operation of a variety of commercial custodial equipment such as a vacuum cleaner, automatic scrubber, high-speed burnisher, single-disc scrubber, carpet extraction/shampoo equipment, or other essential or similar custodial equipment.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Valid driver’s license.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Electrical Hazards&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Inclement Weather&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Driving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Heights&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• For any other related custodial experience, please include any/all related work experience associated with the required qualifications for this position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Change linens, make beds, and bunk/debunk beds.&lt;br&gt;• Check fire extinguishers and related equipment as scheduled; report any deficiencies to the supervisor.&lt;br&gt;• Depending on assignment, may be required to move custodial equipment, fill in for vacant positions, etc.&lt;br&gt;• Disinfect restrooms, showers, and locker rooms.&lt;br&gt;• Empty waste baskets and trash containers and gather and dispose of trash and foreign material from assigned area (to include perimeter of assigned building)&lt;br&gt;• Maintain current knowledge of bloodborne pathogens policies and procedures.&lt;br&gt;• May be responsible for carrying, distributing, and delivering custodial supplies and equipment.&lt;br&gt;• Minimize waste of cleaning, paper, soap, and other supplies.&lt;br&gt;• Open and close buildings, classrooms, offices, etc. of assigned areas.&lt;br&gt;• Remove snow and ice from entrances of assigned areas, apply salt as necessary.&lt;br&gt;• Replace light bulbs, globes, tubes, and light lenses.&lt;br&gt;• Replenish paper and soap products.&lt;br&gt;• Report needed maintenance on assigned equipment.&lt;br&gt;• Report needed repairs to supervisor or call physical plant in emergencies.&lt;br&gt;• Respond to emergency custodial requests (which could include blood and body fluid clean-up).&lt;br&gt;• Set up tables, chairs, and other related furniture as needed.&lt;br&gt;• Sweep, wet mop, refinish hard surface floors, clean carpet, vacuum.&lt;br&gt;• Utilize a household plunger to unplug commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture.&lt;br&gt;• Wash walls, woodwork, windows, blinds, mirrors, bathroom fixtures, furniture, chalk/white boards, and climb ladders.&lt;br&gt;• Work with different cleaning chemicals and equipment and follow procedures for safe handling and use, and wear assigned protective equipment.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;• Operate a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. &lt;br&gt;• Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;• Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;• Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;• Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;• Assist other service workers as needed.&lt;br&gt;• Train and direct others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;• Communicate and work effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors.&lt;br&gt;• Exercise good judgment in resolving situations related to cleaning and proper chemical use, referring unusual problems to the supervisor.&lt;br&gt;• Maintain a high standard of cleanliness and follow safety and disinfecting standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;• Read, understand, and follow instructions, safety and direction labels, equipment operations manuals, etc.&lt;br&gt;• Train and direct others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;• Work harmoniously with and lead others in all situations, including those environments which may involve variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads.&lt;br&gt;• Work independently.&lt;br&gt;• May be required to work in hot, humid areas and/or cold weather environments and/or wear personal protective equipment.&lt;br&gt;• May frequently lift up to 50 lbs. When required to lift, pull, push, etc., heavy objects over 50 pounds, the employee must use good judgment and obtain additional assistance, such as help from a second person or a mechanical means.&lt;br&gt;• Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 14, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498178&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498180</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498180</link><title>Food Service Worker</title><description>A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 1:30pm-10pm Sunday through Wednesday and Saturday.  Days off are Thursday and Friday. This position will begin as soon as possible, subject to manager approval.  However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalency. Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:refNo>498180</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 491px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Food Service Worker&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;51804 - The Rock Cafe&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$17.53 -hourly rate pursuant to the FSU and AFSCME/AFL-CIO Agreement.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Comprehensive benefit package (health care, vacation, etc.). Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/afscme.htm\"&gt;AFSCME Benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Full-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;Custodial, Maintenance, Dining, Skilled Trade (AFSCME Local 1609)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Just Cause&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;A position classified as a Food Service Worker is available with Dining Services at The Rock Cafe. The normal working hours are 1:30pm-10pm Sunday through Wednesday and Saturday. Days off are Thursday and Friday. This position will begin as soon as possible, subject to manager approval. However, the employee may be required to work other times, including evenings and/or weekends. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University’s requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Provide food services support by preparing and serving food, waiting on customers, and maintaining assigned area. Personnel who possess the special qualifications and training necessary for this position may apply. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalency.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Six months full-time equivalent experience in commercial food service to include food preparation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Sitting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Balancing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;As directed, train others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assist other food service employees as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Assure that food is palatable and appetizing.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook and handle food in accordance with safe food-handling and sanitary requirements, following departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Interact with customers and staff in a polite, friendly, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain equipment, pots, pans, utensils, and the work area in a clean, orderly, and sanitary condition, in accordance with departmental sanitation policies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimize food waste.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Obtain foods from storage areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operate various kitchen equipment and machines, utilize utensils.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Perform the work of other Dining Service classifications when assigned.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare food for service and ensure continued availability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Prepare foods using recipes generated from the computerized menu management system.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respond to special dietary requests.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set up and maintain food preparation, serving, and display areas in an attractive and sanitary manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain safety and sanitation standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report to immediate supervisor and/or designee.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Train and direct student employees in performing the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Remove trash, break down cardboard boxes, and assist in the University recycling efforts.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ability to communicate effectively.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ability to interact with the public in a friendly, polite, and courteous manner.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be familiar with seasoning requirements and kitchen equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cook a variety of foods in large and small quantities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Follow safety and sanitation standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Keep accurate records.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow recipes, directions, safety labels, equipment operations manuals, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work harmoniously with others in variable temperatures, close confines, noise, and stressful situations and workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;All applicants must ensure their application information reflects how they meet the minimum qualifications posted in the job posting to be considered for the position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 14, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498180&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498181</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498181</link><title>Part-Time Custodian (Racquet &amp; Fitness Center)</title><description>A position classified as a part-time custodian is available with the Facilities Management department in the Racquet &amp; Fitness Center. The work schedule will be 20 hours per week and will not exceed 28 hours a week. The normal working hours are 10:00 pm - 2:00 am, Monday through Friday. However, work may be required at other times including evenings/weekends. It is not anticipated that this position will become full-time. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University's requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys. Required: High School Diploma or GED equivalent. Valid driver's license. No custodial work experience required – will train selected applicant.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Staff,Part-Time</job:category><job:refNo>498181</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 633px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part-Time Custodian (Racquet &amp;amp; Fitness Center)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids (Main Campus)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;55200 - Bldg Custodial Admin&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.75 per hour&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 78px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 78px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 78px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Please see the following link for a list of benefits offered with this position.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Benefits/parttime.htm\"&gt;Part Time Support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 78px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;FLSA:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Non-Exempt&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Temporary/Continuing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Continuing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Part-Time/Full-Time:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Part-Time&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 16px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 16px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Union Group:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 16px\"&gt;N/A&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 16px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Term of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;12 Month&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;At Will/Just Cause:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;At Will&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;A position classified as a part-time custodian is available with the Facilities Management department in the Racquet &amp;amp; Fitness Center. The work schedule will be 20 hours per week and will not exceed 28 hours a week. The normal working hours are 10:00 pm - 2:00 am, Monday through Friday. However, work may be required at other times including evenings/weekends. It is not anticipated that this position will become full-time. If required by job duties, employee must be able to fulfill the University's requirements concerning issuance and use of University keys.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Staff&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;High school diploma or GED equivalent.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Work Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;No custodial work experience required - will train selected applicant.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Licenses and Certifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Valid driver's license.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Bending&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Carrying&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Electrical Hazards&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Inclement Weather&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Moving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Reaching&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Twisting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Climbing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Driving&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Lifting&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Pulling/Pushing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Repetitive movement&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Standing&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Education/Experiences to be Considered:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Any other related custodial experience. Please include any/all related work experience associated with the required qualifications for this position.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Sweep, wet mop, refinish hard surface floors, clean carpet, and vacuum.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Wash walls, woodwork, windows, blinds, mirrors, bathroom fixtures, furniture, chalk/white boards, and climb ladders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Disinfect restrooms, showers, and locker rooms.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Replenish paper and soap products.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report needed maintenance on assigned equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Replace light bulbs, globes, tubes, and light lenses.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Set up tables, chairs, and other related furniture as needed for class and conference rooms, offices, special events, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Empty waste baskets and trash containers; and gather and dispose of trash and foreign material from assigned area (to include perimeter of assigned area).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Minimize waste of cleaning, paper, soap, and other supplies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Remove snow and ice from entrances of assigned areas; apply salt as necessary.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Report needed repairs to supervisor or call Facilities work control center in emergencies.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Open and close buildings, classrooms, offices, etc. of assigned areas.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Check fire extinguishers and related equipment as scheduled; report any deficiencies to supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain current knowledge of bloodborne pathogen policies and procedures.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Utilize a household plunger to unplug commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Change linens, make beds, and bunk/debunk beds.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Respond to emergency custodial requests (which could include blood and body fluid clean up).&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;May be responsible for carrying, distributing, and delivering custodial supplies and equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work with different cleaning chemicals and equipment, follow procedures for safe handling and use, and wear assigned protective equipment.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Depending on assignment, may be required to move custodial equipment, fill in for vacant positions, etc.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Operates a university or personal vehicle safely while carrying out job responsibilities. Will authorize, pursuant to university policies and procedures, a driving record check, and will meet the driving authorization requirements through the course of employment in a position where you are authorized to drive a vehicle as part of your duties. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Carries out responsibilities in accordance with university policies and applicable laws. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Cultivates an environment of belonging that values, respects, supports, and celebrates individual similarities and differences, allowing students, faculty, and staff to thrive authentically. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support, promote, and develop university student enrollment and retention initiatives. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Any other duties assigned within the position classification area.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marginal Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;Assists other service workers as needed.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Reports to immediate supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintains safety, health, and quality standards in all duties and responsibilities.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintains safety and security of equipment, vehicles, keys, tools, materials, and inventories.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Work and lead others harmoniously in all situations, including those environments which may involve variable temperatures, noise, and stressful workloads.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Maintain a high standard of cleanliness and follow safety and disinfecting standards and practices.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Read, understand, and follow instructions, safety and direction labels, and equipment operation manuals.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ability to train and direct others in the performance of the characteristic duties.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Communicate and work effectively with students, staff, faculty, and visitors.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Work independently.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Exercise good judgment in resolving situations related to cleaning and proper chemical use, referring unusual problems to supervisor.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Demonstrated successful experience working directly with people from diverse backgrounds, including cultural, educational, socioeconomic, and life experiences.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;ul&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Cover Letter&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;li&gt;Resume&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ul&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 34px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 34px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optional Documents:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 34px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Initial Application Review Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;September 14, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open Until Position is Filled?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Yes&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 15px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 15px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Posting Close Date:&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 15px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Click &lt;a title=\"Employment Page\" href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/administration/adminandfinance/human/Employment/homepage.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;here&lt;/a&gt; to learn more about working at FSU and KCAD.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498181&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate></job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Staff</job:workType><job:category>Staff,Part-Time</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498182</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498182</link><title>Facilities - Physical Plant Facility Mgt Assistant (Student Position)</title><description>The Facility Manager Assistant will assist with support functions of our integrated workplace management system Planon.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498182</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 253px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Facilities - Physical Plant Facility Mgt Assistant (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;55- Physical Plant&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;The Facility Manager Assistant will assist with support functions of our integrated workplace management system Planon.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must have strong communication and customer service skills&lt;br&gt;*Knowledgeable in Microsoft&lt;br&gt;*Work experience/academic background in Facility Management is preferred&lt;br&gt;*&lt;span&gt;As an individual who is responsible for driving on behalf of the university, a driving record check will be run pursuant to university policies. The individual will be required to sign an authorization to run a criminal history background and driving record check.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Set-up of HVAC, Electrical, and Plumbing system assets&lt;br&gt;*Creation of preventative maintenance schedule for assets&lt;br&gt;*Update/create user training guides for both Campus and Physical Plant dealing with the various modules of Planon&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 1, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498182&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Wed, 02 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498183</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498183</link><title>Facilities- Project Management (Student Position)</title><description>Are you a student who is pursuing a career in project management? If so, this position will give you hands on experience and will allow you to gain further knowledge in the field.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498183</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 253px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Facilities - Project Management Assistant (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;55- Physical Plant&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Are you a student who is pursuing a career in project management? If so, this position will give you hands on experience and will allow you to gain further knowledge in the field.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must be able to work independently &lt;br&gt;*Must have extensive knowledge of AutoCAD, Revit, Adobe Illustrator, reading construction documents, construction processes, architectural graphics, and field measurements&lt;br&gt;*As an individual who is responsible for driving on behalf of the university, a driving record check will be run pursuant to university policies. The individual will be required to sign an authorization to run a criminal history background and driving record check.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;*Assist and perform highly skilled duties associated with the Project Management Department&lt;br&gt;*Assist with developing project scopes&lt;br&gt;*Prepare bid packages&lt;br&gt;*Research materials and methods&lt;br&gt;*Preparing cost estimates, drawings, and specifications&lt;br&gt;*Implementing and scheduling assigned projects and performing construction management&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;*Performs job duties with the use of a university vehicle&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 1 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498183&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Wed, 02 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498185</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498185</link><title>Digital Media Assistant (Student Position)</title><description>Do you enjoy conducting research on topics regarding the career you are pursuing? If so, this assistant position may be your opportunity to gain more knowledge and experience within your future career.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498185</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 236px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Digital Media Research Assistant (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;College of Business&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00 - $14.49&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Do you enjoy conducting research on topics regarding the career you are pursuing? If so, this assistant position may be your opportunity to gain more knowledge and experience within your future career.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must have a good understanding of the subject matter that is to be researched&lt;br&gt;*Able to complete more intensive work assignments&lt;br&gt;*Possess advances qualifications of this position&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Data collection and management&lt;br&gt;*Using database and spreadsheet programs&lt;br&gt;*Decision-making on issues relevant to data collection&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;5&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498185&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498186</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498186</link><title>Interdisciplinary Clerical 1 (Student Position)</title><description>The Clerical General Level I position will consist of office work and will allow you to expand your knowledge in Microsoft programs and other general office duties.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498186</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 253px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Interdisciplinary Clerical General Level I (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;University College&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73- $13.99&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;The Clerical General Level I position will consist of office work and will allow you to expand your knowledge in Microsoft programs and other general office duties.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Should have knowledge in Microsoft programs such as Word and Excel&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Answering phones, data entry, filing, typing, and photocopying&lt;br&gt;*Manual assembly&lt;br&gt;*Assisting faculty and patrons&lt;br&gt;*Scheduling appointments&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498186&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498190</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498190</link><title>Stage/Auditorium Assistant Level I (Student Position)</title><description>Williams Auditorium is seeking a dependable, motivated student worker to join our event operations team. This position provides hands-on experience in live events, concerts, theater, lectures, conferences, performances, and other programs held at Williams Auditorium. \n\nThis is a great opportunity for students interested in theater, music, event planning, production, communications, hospitality, entertainment, or live events, but no previous technical experience is required.</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-28T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498190</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Stage/Auditorium Assistant Level I (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;College of Arts and Sciences&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Williams Auditorium is seeking a dependable, motivated student worker to join our event operations team. This position provides hands-on experience in live events, concerts, theater, lectures, conferences, performances, and other programs held at Williams Auditorium.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This is a great opportunity for students interested in theater, music, event planning, production, communications, hospitality, entertainment, or live events, but no previous technical experience is required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Required:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Dependable and able to arrive on time for scheduled shifts&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Willingness to learn and work as part of a team&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Ability to follow directions and safety procedures&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Positive and professional attitude&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Ability to perform physical tasks associated with event setup and teardown&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Preferred, but not required:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Interest or experience in theater, music, events, production, or entertainment&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Previous experience with stage equipment, lighting, audio, or video&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Customer service or hospitality experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Ability to work independently once trained&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Student workers may assist with a wide variety of tasks, including:&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Setting up and tearing down events&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Moving and arranging tables, chairs, staging, and other equipment&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Assisting with stage and backstage preparations&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Helping with basic lighting, audio, and video equipment&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Assisting with microphones and presentation equipment&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Supporting concerts, theater productions, lectures, conferences, ceremonies, and special events&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Assisting performers, speakers, presenters, and event clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Helping with audience seating and event logistics&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Preparing dressing rooms, backstage areas, and event spaces&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Operating or assisting with basic venue equipment after appropriate training&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Loading and unloading event equipment and materials&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Maintaining clean, organized, and safe event spaces&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Assisting with event transitions and room changes&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Providing general event support before, during, and after events&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Following venue safety procedures and event-specific instructions&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Performing other duties related to auditorium and event operations as assigned&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;• Scenic Construction and/ or painting assistance for university productions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Cover Letter&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498190&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498164</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498164</link><title>Violence Prevent Peer Educator (Student Position)</title><description>The Anti-Violence Alliance office is seeking a student to assist with creating new prevention initiatives and amplifying existing efforts on campus. This position is relevant for students pursuing degrees in communications, criminal justice, graphic design, social sciences, or women's studies.</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-27T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498164</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 106.271%; height: 236px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 17px\"&gt;Violence Prevention Peer Educator (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.4647%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;60- VP Student Affairs&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73 - $14.00&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%\"&gt;The Anti-Violence Alliance office is seeking a student to assist with creating new prevention initiatives and amplifying existing efforts on campus. This position is relevant for students pursuing degrees in communications, criminal justice, graphic design, social sciences, or women's studies.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must display a commitment to sexual and relationship violence issues&lt;br&gt;*A passion and desire to make a difference&lt;br&gt;*Have a desire to learn about university prevention organizations and practices&lt;br&gt;*Must be organized, have strong attention to detail, and be able to complete projects independently&lt;br&gt;*Be enrolled at Ferris State University, taking at least 6 credits&lt;br&gt;*Maintain at least a 2.0 GPA&lt;br&gt;*Have approval from the Office of Student Community Standards to join the program&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Generate a curriculum of events that would occur throughout the academic year&lt;br&gt;*Provide year-round awareness to ensure that changes in thoughts and actions are sustained long-term&lt;br&gt;*Attend all monthly Anti-Violence Alliance meetings&lt;br&gt;*Attend all mandatory training sessions (Including but not limited to dating/domestic violence, sexual assault, stalking, public speaking, prevention best practices, how to facilitate the Bringing in the Bystander curriculum, and annual refresher training )&lt;br&gt;* Co-facilitate prevention/awareness programs or events each semester&lt;br&gt;*We are looking mainly for peer educators who are willing to present, but we can accept a few applicants who only want to create social media content.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 35px\"&gt;3&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 18px\"&gt;09/16/2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.5353%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.4647%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity, and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498164&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Thu, 17 Sep 2026 03:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>E - Student Affairs</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498165</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498165</link><title>Violence Prevent Peer Educator (Student Position)</title><description>The Anti-Violence Alliance office is seek