ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498051</link><title>Athletic Camp Asst II (Student Position)</title><description>This position works with the Athletic camps.</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-04T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498051</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 219px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Athletic Camp Asst II (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;50 - Admin and Finance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00 - $14.49&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must posses a high level of skill and exercise independent judgement&lt;br&gt;*Must be able to prioritize and perform tasks with great attention to detail and perform independently with minimal supervision &lt;br&gt;*Personal accountability for the operation of the camp they are involved with&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Independent working with campers and instructing &lt;br&gt;*Supervising counselors on and off during camp duties&lt;br&gt;*Possibly working with campers overnight in the housing area&lt;br&gt;*Responsible for developing, coordinating, and implementing camp activities&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498051&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>D - Admin and Finance</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497907</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497907</link><title>Center Tutor 1 (Student Position)</title><description>A center tutor provides academic support to students in a variety of subject areas, excluding writing, within the campus Tutoring Center. This role involves assisting students during scheduled center hours by explaining course material and reviewing concepts to promote academic success.\n\nThe Center Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.\n\nThis position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.\n\nThis position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.\n\nStudent employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>497907</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Center Tutor - Level I (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Retention and Student Success&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;A center tutor provides academic support to students in a variety of subject areas, excluding writing, within the campus Tutoring Center. This role involves assisting students during scheduled center hours by explaining course material and reviewing concepts to promote academic success.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Center Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Student employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must have a GPA of 2.75 or higher&lt;br&gt;*Must have completed the course they will be assisting with and earned a grade of B or higher&lt;br&gt;*For math tutoring, must have completed Math 130&lt;br&gt;*Must demonstrate excellent communication and organizational skills&lt;br&gt;*Must be hired through HR prior to beginning tutoring duties&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Will assist students with coursework in various subject areas&lt;br&gt;*May be required to provide virtual tutoring during scheduled shifts in the Tutoring Center or other approved University site, as needed&lt;br&gt;*Center tutors will reach out to faculty of the courses they support to inform them of their scheduled availability to provide tutoring assistance to students&lt;br&gt;*Center tutors are required to document a summary of each appointment in Navigate 360 after every tutoring session&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule, Cover Letter (optional)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 18, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=497907&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497908</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497908</link><title>Classroom Tutor 1 (Student Position)</title><description>A classroom tutor supports students in a specific class by working with faculty to reinforce course content, answer questions, and clarify difficult concepts during class time. The tutor is required to attend all class sessions and be present in the location where the course is held.\n\nThe Classroom Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.\n\nThis position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.\n\nThis position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.\n\nStudent employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>497908</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Classroom Tutor - Level I (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Retention and Student Success&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73- $13.99&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;A classroom tutor supports students in a specific class by working with faculty to reinforce course content, answer questions, and clarify difficult concepts during class time. The tutor is required to attend all class sessions and be present in the location where the course is held.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Classroom Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Student employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must have a GPA of 2.75 or better&lt;br&gt;*Have completed the course they are assisting with and received a B or better&lt;br&gt;*If tutoring in Math courses, must have completed math 130&lt;br&gt;*Excellent communication skills and organization&lt;br&gt;*Must be hired through HR prior to beginning tutoring duties&lt;br&gt;* Student classroom tutor does not exceed 8 hours a day&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Assist students with course work in various subject areas&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 18, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=497908&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497909</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497909</link><title>Workshop Tutor 1 (Student Position)</title><description>A workshop tutor provides academic support through workshop sessions focused on specific courses or topics. This role involves leading or assisting workshops that review key concepts, reinforce course material, and help students prepare for assignments and exams. Workshop tutors help students learn by providing focused, interactive learning activities in a group setting. Workshops take place in a classroom provided by the department or professor for up to two hours per day.\n\nThe Workshop Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.\n\nThis position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.\n\nThis position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.\n\nStudent employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>497909</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Workshop Tutor 1 (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;University College&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;A workshop tutor provides academic support through workshop sessions focused on specific courses or topics. This role involves leading or assisting workshops that review key concepts, reinforce course material, and help students prepare for assignments and exams. Workshop tutors help students learn by providing focused, interactive learning activities in a group setting. Workshops take place in a classroom provided by the department or professor for up to two hours per day.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Workshop Tutor provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Student employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Student&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must have a GPA of 2.75 or higher&lt;br&gt;*Must have completed the course they will be assisting with and earned a grade of B or higher&lt;br&gt;*For math tutoring, must have completed Math 130&lt;br&gt;*Must demonstrate excellent communication and organizational skills&lt;br&gt;*Must be hired through HR prior to beginning tutoring duties&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Will assist students with coursework in various subject areas in a workshop setting&lt;br&gt;*For questions or concerns outside of the position summary requested by faculty, please direct your questions to the Director&lt;br&gt;*Workshop tutors are required to take attendance in Navigate for every workshop tutoring session&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule, Cover Letter (optional)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 18, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=497909&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497910</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497910</link><title>SLA Facilitator (Student Position)</title><description>The Structured Learning Assistance (SLA) Facilitator reports directly to the Director and supports courses identified as high-risk for failure by working collaboratively with faculty and students to promote academic success. The facilitator leads regularly scheduled workshops (up to 1 hour and 15 minutes per session) that reinforce course concepts, encourage active and collaborative learning, and help students successfully complete coursework. Responsibilities may include attending class sessions, communicating with instructors, tracking attendance and student progress, and developing engaging, course-specific\nlearning activities. The SLA Facilitator serves as a mentor and academic resource, helping students build confidence, strengthen study strategies, and develop independent learning skills.\n\nThe SLA Facilitator provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.\n\nThis position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.\n\nThis position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of SLA facilitation to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.\n\nStudent employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>497910</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 253px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;SLA Facilitator (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Structured Learning Assistance&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The Structured Learning Assistance (SLA) Facilitator reports directly to the Director and supports courses identified as high-risk for failure by working collaboratively with faculty and students to promote academic success. The facilitator leads regularly scheduled workshops (up to 1 hour and 15 minutes per session) that reinforce course concepts, encourage active and collaborative learning, and help students successfully complete coursework. Responsibilities may include attending class sessions, communicating with instructors, tracking attendance and student progress, and developing engaging, course-specific&lt;br&gt;learning activities. The SLA Facilitator serves as a mentor and academic resource, helping students build confidence, strengthen study strategies, and develop independent learning skills.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The SLA Facilitator provides supplemental academic support through tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;This position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of SLA facilitation to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Student employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;The requirements listed below are: representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Any equivalent combination of education, training, and experience, which provides the required&lt;br&gt;knowledge, abilities, and skills, may be considered. Reasonable accommodations may be&lt;br&gt;made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Education/Skills&lt;br&gt;Minimum: Two years of college, or an Associate Degree, or Comparable work-related&lt;br&gt;experience in subject area, or Teaching, training or tutoring experience.&lt;br&gt;Excellent public speaking and communication skills. Good time&lt;br&gt;management and organizational skills. Ability to enforce program rules and&lt;br&gt;policies. In depth knowledge of subject material.&lt;br&gt;Preferred: Bachelor’s Degree, or Upper-level BS student in subject content area with&lt;br&gt;over 3.5 GPA. Experience with SLA workshops.&lt;br&gt;Ability to:&lt;br&gt;1.) Interact successfully with faculty, students, and staff from a diverse population.&lt;br&gt;2.) Meet deadlines in a timely manner.&lt;br&gt;3.) Model professional behavior and skills commonly attributed to successful students.&lt;br&gt;4.) Maintain an organized course/workshop notebook.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Work Experience&lt;br&gt;Minimum: Two years or college or related relevant work experience.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Reports directly to the Director&lt;br&gt;*Responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of designated information&lt;br&gt;*Organize and facilitate weekly SLA workshops, including clarifying course concepts, incorporating study skills, generating notes from course lectures/labs, and preparing workshop materials&lt;br&gt;*Meeting with course faculty and the director, adhering to program policies, and maintaining appropriate workshop records as instructed&lt;br&gt;*Responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of designated information&lt;br&gt;*Performs all duties in compliance with applicable university policies and procedures, as well as state and federal requirements&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule, Cover Letter (Optional)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Special Instructions to Applicants:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=497910&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497990</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497990</link><title>Pharmacology Research Assistant (Student Position)</title><description>This position will be supported by Md Afjalus Siraj, PhD Ferris Research Grant, 2026. The student Research Assistant will work on how combination therapy, like SMNDC1 inhibitor along with KRAS inhibitor, overcome targeted therapy resistance in pancreatic cancer.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>497990</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Pharmacology Research Assistant (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;College of Pharmacy&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;This position will be supported by Md Afjalus Siraj, PhD Ferris Research Grant, 2026. The student Research Assistant will work on how combination therapy, like SMNDC1 inhibitor along with KRAS inhibitor, overcome targeted therapy resistance in pancreatic cancer.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Current student of Ferris State University with a major in Forensic Biology, Biotechnology, Biochemistry&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;Design and revise laboratory protocols&lt;br&gt;In hand cell based assay development&lt;br&gt;Lab note maintenance and regular discussion with PI&lt;br&gt;Attend weekly lab meeting&lt;br&gt;Discuss with PI about other weekly responsibilities&lt;br&gt;Literature review and data extraction&lt;br&gt;Data analysis&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Cover Letter&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 12, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=497990&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sun, 13 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497994</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/497994</link><title>Standby Center Tutor 1 (Student Position)</title><description>A standby center tutor supports students who need academic assistance across various subject areas. This role involves providing tutoring during the Tutoring Center's operational hours on an as-needed basis.\nStandby tutoring means tutors are hired based on potential needs and are available on demand. Standby tutors are not guaranteed hours but are expected to be available when there is a need or demand for on-site tutoring.\nFor example, if a student needs help with a specific course and a standby tutor has availability in Navigate, the student can schedule a tutoring session. The tutor will receive an email nomination and then meet the student in the Tutoring Center to provide academic support.\n\nThe Standby Center Tutor provides supplemental academic support through\ntutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.\n\nThis position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.\n\nThis position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.\n\nStudent employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>497994</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Standby Center Tutor 1 (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px; width: 72.561%\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;University College&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;A standby center tutor supports students who need academic assistance across various subject areas. This role involves providing tutoring during the Tutoring Center's operational hours on an as-needed basis. &lt;br&gt;Standby tutoring means tutors are hired based on potential needs and are available on demand. Standby tutors are not guaranteed hours but are expected to be available when there is a need or demand for on-site tutoring.&lt;br&gt;For example, if a student needs help with a specific course and a standby tutor has availability in Navigate, the student can schedule a tutoring session. The tutor will receive an email nomination and then meet the student in the Tutoring Center to provide academic support.&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;The Standby Center Tutor provides supplemental academic support through&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;tutoring activities designed to reinforce course concepts and aid student mastery of course content.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;This position supports, but does not replace, instructional faculty.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;This position is not eligible for remote work. All compensated work must be performed from an approved university location. The position may include virtual delivery of tutoring to students; however, virtual delivery must occur while the student employee is physically working from an approved university location.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;div&gt;Student employees in this role are not instructors and may not perform duties reserved for instructional faculty, including creating or revising syllabi, designing or assigning graded coursework, assessing learning for grades, grading student work, managing Canvas or other LMS course functions, delivering required instruction on behalf of faculty, substituting for faculty, making course policy decisions, or completing compensated work already assigned to instructional faculty. The role is limited to supplemental academic support, facilitation of learning activities, and student-success support.&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Type:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Student&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Must have a GPA of 2.75 or higher&lt;br&gt;*Must have completed the course they will be assisting with and earned a grade of B or higher&lt;br&gt;*For math tutoring, must have completed Math 130&lt;br&gt;*Must demonstrate excellent communication and organizational skills&lt;br&gt;*Must be hired through HR prior to beginning tutoring duties&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Will assist students with coursework in various subject areas&lt;br&gt;*May be required to provide virtual tutoring, as needed&lt;br&gt;*May be required to provide virtual tutoring as needed while working on site in the Tutoring Center&lt;br&gt;*Standby tutoring is on-demand support based on student need. If a student schedules a session in&lt;br&gt;Navigate and a tutor is available, the tutor receives an email confirmation and meets the student in the Tutoring Center to provide assistance&lt;br&gt;*Standby tutors are not guaranteed hours but are expected to be available as needed for on-site tutoring.&lt;br&gt;*Standby tutors will reach out to faculty of the courses they support to inform them of their availability to provide tutoring assistance to students&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;10&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume, Class Schedule, Cover Letter (optional)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;December 18, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=497994&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2026 04:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>C - VPAA</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498040</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498040</link><title>Registrar Clerical Level 2 (Student Position)</title><description>Do you have experience in Clerical General Level I? If so, this position of Clerical General Level II may be your opportunity to continue growing your knowledge in the office setting.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498040</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 236px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Registrar Clerical General Level II (Student Position)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI 49307&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Enrollment Services&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$14.00- $14.49&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Do you have experience in Clerical General Level I? If so, this position of Clerical General Level II may be your opportunity to continue growing your knowledge in the office setting.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;*Previous experience in an office setting&lt;br&gt;*Are knowledgeable in necessary computer operations and office policies and procedures&lt;br&gt;*Have knowledge in Microsoft programs such as Word and Excel&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;*Answering the phone, data entry, filing, typing, and photocopying&lt;br&gt;*Assisting faculty and patrons&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;2&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documents Needed to Apply:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Resume/ Class Schedule&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Close Date:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;September 7, 2026&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EEO Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Ferris State University, an Affirmative Action/Equal Opportunity employer, is committed to enhancing equity, inclusion, and diversity within its community. Ferris offers employment opportunities to qualified candidates seeking careers in a student-focused environment that values opportunity, collaboration, diversity and educational excellence.&amp;nbsp; Learn more about the Ferris Mission and community at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"http://ferris.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;ferris.edu&lt;/a&gt;. The University actively seeks applications from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, veterans, and other underrepresented groups. For more information on the University’s Policy on Non-Discrimination, visit:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=\"https://www.ferris.edu/HTMLS/administration/president/generalcounsel/pdfs-docs/00108985.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"&gt;Ferris Non-Discrimination Statement&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;/tbody&gt;\n&lt;/table&gt;</job:description><job:applyLink>https://secure.dc4.pageuppeople.com/apply/1010/gateway/default.aspx?c=apply&amp;lJobID=498040&amp;lJobSourceTypeID=796&amp;sLanguage=en-us</job:applyLink><job:closingDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 03:55:00 GMT</job:closingDate><job:location>Big Rapids, MI 49307</job:location><job:workType>Student Employment - General</job:workType><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:subCategory></job:subCategory><job:businessLayer1>E - Student Affairs</job:businessLayer1></item><item><guid isPermaLink=\"true\">https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498041</guid><link>https://jobs.ferris.edu/cw/en-us/job/498041</link><title>Machine Tool Stockroom Assista (Student Position)</title><description>Check in and out tools, maintain inventory, for Manufacturing Engineering Machining Laboratory Tool Crib. Assist faculty in various duties related to Machining Laboratory, assist students in machining process, practice safe working habits.</description><pubDate>Mon, 03 Aug 2026 04:00:00 Z</pubDate><a10:updated>2026-08-03T04:00:00Z</a10:updated><job:category>Student Employment - General</job:category><job:refNo>498041</job:refNo><job:description>&lt;table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 93.6673%; height: 453px\" border=\"1\"&gt;\n&lt;tbody&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Title:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Machine Tool Stockroom Assistant (Student Posting)&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Big Rapids, MI&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 46px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Department:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"height: 46px\"&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;College of Engineering Technology&lt;/p&gt;\n&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 46px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advertised Salary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;$13.73- $13.99&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary of Position:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Check in and out tools, maintain inventory, for Manufacturing Engineering Machining Laboratory Tool Crib. Assist faculty in various duties related to Machining Laboratory, assist students in machining process, practice safe working habits.&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 17px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 17px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 17px\"&gt;Student must have previously taken manufacturing courses within the Manufacturing Engineering program&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 17px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 18px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 18px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Duties/Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 18px\"&gt;knowledge of feed and speed calculations, safe working habits, measuring instruments, and CNC programing&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 18px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"height: 35px\"&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 27.439%; height: 35px\"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Positions Available:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 72.561%; height: 35px\"&gt;1&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;td style=\"width: 6.27132%; height: 35px\"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/td&gt;\n&lt;/tr&gt;\n&lt;tr style=\"heig